      "paragraph_text": "P5 — generated transfer practice. For $`x\\gt 0`$, find the derivative of $`y=x^x`$. Explain why inserting $`r=x`$ into the constant-power rule $`(x^r)'=rx^{r-1}`$ is not justified. A complete response states a representation or logarithmic equation that keeps the varying exponent visible, differentiates it, and gives the derivative in terms of $`x`$. [Hint P5](hints.md#h5) · [Solution P5](solutions.md#s5)\n",
