      "paragraph_sha256": "38a94330dd66a8a7da638502dc2e30d350405f660f1d330e1940ea3e1b7ba0f6",
      "paragraph_text": "Differentiate $`xy`$ as $`1\\cdot y+xy'`$. The derivative of $`y^2`$ is $`2yy'`$. Put terms containing $`y'`$ on one side, factor out $`y'`$, then substitute the point. A tangent of slope $`m`$ through $`(1,2)`$ has equation $`y-2=m(x-1)`$. [Return to P3](lesson.md#p3)\n",
