      "paragraph_sha256": "85812ef908b3229182543436ecfdd8ee7926b5c2233d2100bb14593df4e8881b",
      "paragraph_text": "P062. To assemble the branches: on the left, begin just below the horizontal axis and descend, becoming steeper, toward negative infinity near $`0^-`$. On the right, begin at arbitrarily negative heights near $`0^+`$, rise through $`(1,0)`$ to the maximum $`(2,1/4)`$, and then descend toward the horizontal asymptote from above. The descending branch is concave down until $`(3,2/9)`$ and concave up afterward, so after that point its negative slope becomes less negative. Leave a gap at zero. This description accounts for every domain interval and distinguishes the maximum at $`2`$ from the inflection at $`3`$. [Return to Task C](#task-c) · [Hints](#hints) · [Start](#start).\n",
